{%- comment -%}
  Shipping, refund, privacy, terms. The theme had no policy template at all, so
  Shopify dropped the raw policy HTML straight into the layout with nothing
  around it — full window width, no measure, no type scale, headings and lists
  falling back to browser defaults. On a site where everything else is set in
  Fraunces and Assistant it looked like a different website.

  Same treatment as a page: reading measure, .rte typography, and a link back
  so the policy isn't a dead end.
{%- endcomment -%}

<div class="container">
  <div class="page-content">
    <h1 class="page-content__title">{{ policy.title }}</h1>

    <div class="rte page-content__body">
      {{ policy.body }}
    </div>

    <p class="page-content__back">
      <a href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}">&larr; Back to the buttons</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
